# A Unity project carries its own .gitignore. The shared ktsu.Sdk one deliberately does not try to
# be a Unity .gitignore: the folders below are only generated caches when they sit beside Assets/
# and ProjectSettings/, and ignoring names this generic repo-wide would catch unrelated
# directories - this repository's own examples/demos/Library among them.
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Uu]serSettings/

# Two rules in the shared .gitignore would otherwise swallow Unity source. Both are generic
# .NET/Visual Studio rules that predate any engine support:
#
#   **/[Pp]ackages/*  - meant for a NuGet restore folder, but Unity's Packages/ is project source
#                       and both the manifest and the resolved lock file belong in the repository.
#   *.meta            - meant for the Visual Studio C++ build artifact, but Unity generates one
#                       .meta per asset carrying the GUID that scenes and prefabs reference.
#
# The packaged .gitignore now carries the same negations for consumers, but they cannot be relied
# on here: examples/.gitignore is generated, and the SDK's _KtsuSyncStyleConfigFiles target
# rewrites it from whichever ktsu.Sdk version examples/global.json pins - today a published one
# that predates those negations. A .gitignore this deep in the tree wins over both copies of the
# rule and is nobody's build output.
!Packages/manifest.json
!Packages/packages-lock.json
!Assets/**/*.meta
